been recently made to make it habitable, at least temporarily.  Holes in the
ceiling are patched with strips of oiled canvas nailed over them, and the
windows are covered in much the same way, giving the room a dim feeling.  A
firepit has been dug in the center of the room, with embers still glowing
dully amidst the charred remains of fuel and wood.
