"Steps to an Old Cathedral"
"Here, at the top of the steps, the cathedral is hugely present.  The path here
is worn smooth from much use, although the surrounding shrubs begin to
encroach on the sides of the path.  South the hill rises steeply, while to the
north the wall of the cathedral looms.  Huge blocks of granite have been
transported here and locked together immovably, forming a towering structure.
High up in the walls, huge stained-glass windows are set.  Somehow they have
withstood the tests of time and age.
"
